{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Searches, Etc.","html":"<article id='sn46.111-120'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Saṁyutta Nikāya 46.111–120 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Linked Discourses 46.111–120 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>12. Esanāvagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>12. Searches </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Esanādisutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Searches, Etc. </span></h1></header>\n<p><span class='root'>“Tisso imā, bhikkhave, esanā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Mendicants, there are these three searches. </span>\n<span class='root'>Katamā tisso? </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What three? </span>\n<span class='root'>Kāmesanā, bhavesanā, brahmacariyesanā”ti vitthāretabbaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>The search for sensual pleasures, the search for continued existence, and the search for a spiritual path. …” </span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Esanāvaggo dvādasamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Esanā vidhā āsavo, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Bhavo ca dukkhatā tisso; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Khilaṁ malañca nīgho ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Vedanā taṇhā tasināya cāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='expansion-instructions'><span class='root'>(Bojjhaṅgasaṁyuttassa esanāpeyyālaṁ vivekanissitato vitthāretabbaṁ.) </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>(Tell in full as in SN 45.161–170.) </span></p></article>"}
